      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-214907",
        "knowledge_point_id": "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5",
        "knowledge_point": "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/cb311261eabb4b5c1b6c4114c92e798f0caf2e326dc90486429d230167f6978b.png)\n\nExpress the shaded region above as an inequality.The shaded region above is described by the inequality\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
        "worked_solution": "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-2,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-2.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-2.\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
            "type": "select",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
