        "knowledge_point": "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/75a7f3bfae55a97fbc0c05e2e0356d21de6ceabcc82ac3e1c965838a636f5ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?",
        "worked_solution": "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
