        "reasoning": "All 16 questions agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-142112: x+2y≤4 rearranges to y≤−x/2+2, giving a solid boundary and shading below, option 1. q-143098: dividing −2y≥−3x+6 by −2 reverses the inequality, giving y≤3x/2−3, option 4. The worked-solution images for these two questions depict the same regions as the selected current images. q-214907: the dashed vertical boundary is x=−2 and shading is to its right, so x>−2; the intercept marker does not change the dashed boundary convention. q-215437: the solid boundary is x=−1 and shading is to its left, so x≤−1. q-47367: the limit at 1 is 1 but f(1)=2, so the function is neither continuous nor differentiable there and is not differentiable throughout (−2,2); only III is true. q-73260: differentiability at 4 implies continuity there, and a corner at 2 prevents differentiability; continuity at 0 does not guarantee differentiability, so I and II only. q-52413: both boundaries are solid and the region is above both, giving y≥3x+1 and y≥2. q-90174: shading below both solid lines gives the downward wedge, option 1. q-90323: the region is below the steep dashed line and above the shallow dashed line, giving y<4x+3 and y>x/4−2. q-52461: the region is below both dashed lines, giving y<2x+6 and y<5. q-90327: the region is below the solid increasing line and above the dashed decreasing line, giving y≤x+2 and y>−x+2. q-29384: the region is above both lines, with a strict inequality for the dashed increasing line and an inclusive inequality for the solid decreasing line. q-90054: the region is above both dashed lines, giving x+y>3 and y>2x. q-110078: the region lies above x+2y=−8 and below y=x/2+1, with both boundaries included. q-71662: c·d=4 and d·d=19, so the projection is (4/19)d=⟨4/19,12/19,−12/19⟩. q-24490: the double-angle identity gives cos(10π/3), whose value is −1/2. No submitted grades are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
