        "knowledge_point": "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/3905dacc3977857933a48ced329fc245b357f732aec520e67998efc0b5d7cdab.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?",
        "worked_solution": "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
