        "math_academy_id": "q-71662",
        "knowledge_point_id": "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components",
        "problem": "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{19}⟨1,3,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{19},\\frac{12}{19},-\\frac{12}{19}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
